      "writtenOn": "2019-06-24T18:22:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking closer, if we want to reuse the framework defined in \"battery_fuel_gauge.h\", I don\u0027t find an easy way to reduce code redundancy. If we don\u0027t include \"battery_fuel_gauge.h\" and define board-specific board_batt_params, we may make batt_info a pointer in batt_params and let c424 and c436 share the same batt_info. However, if we go this route, we\u0027ll also need to add code for battery-cut-off-related functions. So this way probably ends up not saving code either.\n\nAnyway, sorry for the confusion, I agree we should just land the initial patch set.",
      "parentUuid": "2a1f786c_f86f636f",
